type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-27"
title: "SEC Filings Tone: topic tone profiles of S&P 500 10-K filings, FY2019–FY2026"
abstract: >-
  Code, labels and results for measuring how S&P 500 companies write about 13 topics (AI, China,
  tariffs, interest rates, supply chain and others) in their 10-K filings from FY2019 to FY2026.
  Hybrid retrieval (OpenAI text-embedding-3-large and BM25) selects passages from Item 1A and
  Item 7 of 3,458 10-Ks; Claude Haiku 5.5 scores 126,051 passages on five dimensions (polarity,
  magnitude, realization, uncertainty, specificity), with FinBERT and the Loughran-McDonald
  dictionary as baselines. The tests were fixed in advance and are reported whether they passed or
  not: on one person's blind labels only realization meets the agreement bar (weighted kappa 0.67),
  and the planned event test against unaffected sectors detects 0 of 11 expected changes. Includes
  a 40-item human-labeled gold set, a retrieval eval, a boilerplate (year-over-year carryover)
  analysis and a cited Q&A layer over the filings.
